From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Sun, 26 Jul 2026 20:29:06 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: hold RCU read lock in all-STA info event handler

mt7996_mcu_rx_all_sta_info_event() dereferences wcid pointers via
mt76_wcid_ptr() (an rcu_dereference) without an RCU read-side
critical section, racing station teardown and crashing on station
stats updates. Upstream already holds the lock in the neighbouring
mt7996_mcu_get_per_sta_info().

Fixes: SDG-2921

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt7996/mcu.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/mt7996/mcu.c
+++ b/mt7996/mcu.c
@@ -848,6 +848,7 @@ mt7996_mcu_rx_all_sta_info_event(struct
 	if (sta_num > (skb->len - sizeof(*res)) / elem_size)
 		sta_num = (skb->len - sizeof(*res)) / elem_size;
 
+	rcu_read_lock();
 	for (i = 0; i < sta_num; i++) {
 		u8 ac;
 		bool v1;
@@ -966,6 +967,7 @@ mt7996_mcu_rx_all_sta_info_event(struct
 			break;
 		}
 	}
+	rcu_read_unlock();
 }
 
 static void
